<title>HONG KONG: Orient Telecom H1 net loss HK$39.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Orient Telecom H1 net loss HK$39.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   19.0 loss  vs 16.8 gain (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  6.10 loss  vs 9.00 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    39.70 loss vs 35.25 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     326.69     vs 250.79</p>
<p>    Company name		 Orient Telecom &amp; Technology</p>
<p>				     Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Orient Telecom &amp; Technology provides network telephone services in Bangkok, generates electricity in China's Shenyang, and is involved in development property in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on provision for diminution in value of a long term investment.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted for 10-into-1 share consolidation.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
